<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Swedish translation.

    A translation of `values/strings.xml`, which is the source (SPEC §9). It
    serves the two Swedish networks of the catalogue — Donkey Republic in
    Malmö and Lundahoj in Lund — and, like every other language here, any
    other city the reader installs. Where Android's own Swedish has a word,
    that word is used; the arbiter is the phone itself.

    Rules, the same as everywhere: positional placeholders, <plurals> for
    anything that agrees, and the `name` attributes left untouched. Swedish
    distinguishes two plural categories, `one` and `other`.

    The typography is Swedish: quotation marks are ” ”, closing on both
    sides, and the dash that breaks a sentence is – with a space on either
    side rather than the em dash the English file uses. A trailing ellipsis is
    written with a space before it — ”Söker …” — which is what Android's own
    Swedish does on every progress message (`android:loading`,
    `settings:wifi_connecting`). Nothing needs escaping: no straight
    apostrophe is written anywhere in the file. Compounds are one word, which
    is what lengthens the labels; where a button could not carry the literal
    translation it takes the shorter wording Android itself uses. The reader
    is addressed as `du`, the only address modern Swedish has, and the
    impersonal turns of the English are kept impersonal.
    See docs/sv-glossary.md.
-->
